# Distribution / packaging
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
release/
tmp/
.worktrees/

# .NET build output for the shared desktop updater.
# These 200+ binaries were tracked, so EVERY `dotnet build` dirtied the tree and
# tripped the release dirty-tree gate -- which trains people into -AllowDirty and
# defeats the gate. build_updater.ps1 regenerates them via `dotnet publish`, and the
# artifact that actually ships is installer/updater/MonClubDesktopUpdater.exe,
# which stays tracked.
updater/**/bin/
updater/**/obj/
# MB2000 script-lab output written on the gym PC (script 12 run logs, script 10
# device backups, the local template store, the saved device config). Operator data
# and device identifiers -- never part of a commit.
tools/mb2000_scripts/logs/
tools/mb2000_scripts/backups/
tools/mb2000_scripts/templates/
tools/mb2000_scripts/config.json
